BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big Bend: check Chisos Basin campsite + backcountry permit windows 
 (reminder only)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261101T093000
DTSTAMP:20261002T180000Z
UID:big-bend-772f9af809@bookdayparks.example
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=1
DESCRIPTION:This is a reminder, not a booking. Once a month, take a look at
  Big Bend National Park campsite and backcountry permit windows.\n\nCHISOS
  BASIN CAMPGROUND (60 sites): reservation only\, no first-come camping. Ab
 out two-thirds of sites open 6 months ahead. Sites 8-10\, 12-15\, 31\, 37 
 and 48-60 open 14 days ahead. New dates open daily at 9:00 AM Central (10:
 00 AM Eastern) on Recreation.gov (time seen on the Seasons & Booking tab\,
  2026-10-01). Book here: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/23
 4038\n\nBACKCOUNTRY PERMITS (Chisos backpacking\, primitive roadside\, des
 ert backpacking): required for all backcountry camping\, $10 per night. So
 me Chisos and roadside sites can normally be booked on Recreation.gov up t
 o 180 days ahead. As of NPS page update 2026-07-20\, all backcountry permi
 ts are in person only at Panther Junction Visitor Center\, up to 24 hours 
 ahead (8:30 AM-5:00 PM daily)\, until further notice. Details: https://www
 .nps.gov/bibe/planyourvisit/bc_usepermits.htm\n\nHOW TO USE: this event re
 peats on the 1st of each month. The monthly reminder is a nudge to check\,
  not the moment a particular night opens. If you know your dates\, count b
 ack 6 months (or 14 days) and set your own 9:00 AM Central alarm. Chisos B
 asin construction runs about two years from spring 2026\, so check NPS ale
 rts.\n\nDates and rules change. Confirm on Recreation.gov and nps.gov befo
 re you book. Not affiliated with NPS or Recreation.gov.
BEGIN:VALARM
